{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uyauw4uoe3zdviz3vfimq54sdh56ozrsdlb4lg5jmnqnnxwlg3na","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RNpk8vfE3rgPHmXmZZ83H8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QQSMlQ; cat >> $R/translation/SYMBOLS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Rust-only extra exports\n\n`nm -D` on the Rust cdylib is a strict superset of the C union.  The only\nconfiguration where it is a *proper* superset is the shake backend, where the\nRust port supplies the 15 entry points that `lib/shake/include/fips202.h`\ndeclares but `lib/shake/src/fips202.c` never defines:\n\n```\nshake128 shake128_absorb shake128_squeezeblocks\nshake128_inc_init shake128_inc_absorb shake128_inc_finalize shake128_inc_squeeze\nsha3_256 sha3_256_inc_init sha3_256_inc_absorb sha3_256_inc_finalize\nsha3_512 sha3_512_inc_init sha3_512_inc_absorb sha3_512_inc_finalize\n```\n\nThey have no C counterpart, so they cannot be differentially tested; see the\nnote at the end of `CONFIGS.md`.  Symbol parity (C ⊆ Rust) is unaffected.\n\n## `libsphincs_core.so` vs `libsphincs_core_det.so`\n\nThe only difference is which `randombytes` implementation is linked:\n\n| | `randombytes` |\n|---|---|\n| `libsphincs_core_det.so` (`rng.c`) | `int randombytes(unsigned char*, unsigned long long)` -- AES-256-CTR-DRBG, deterministic, also exports `randombytes_init`, `seedexpander`, `seedexpander_init`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`, `AES256_ECB`, `DRBG_ctx` |\n| `libsphincs_core.so` (`randombytes.c`) | `void randombytes(unsigned char*, unsigned long long)` -- reads `/dev/urandom` |\n\nThe Rust `[lib] name = \"sphincs_core_det\"` selects the deterministic variant,\nso `rng.rs` owns the exported `randombytes`; `randombytes.rs` is the translation\nof the `/dev/urandom` variant and is deliberately **not** `#[no_mangle]`\n(exporting it would collide).  This introduces no missing symbol: the *name*\n`randombytes` is exported either way.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Append notes to SYMBOLS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6479,"cache_read_input_tokens":363265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6479,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12fe76c7-0bad-40ec-b466-7d674d7f0750","uuid":"4bbcb327-2aed-4b73-986e-4daa18ea7ad1","timestamp":"2026-09-04T16:03:31.387Z"}
